# ssh client config  ->  ~/.ssh/config
#
# In the repo because it is real config: AddKeysToAgent is what makes the key passphrase a
# once-per-boot event rather than once per push, and losing it would be a silent
# regression in ergonomics with no obvious cause.
#
# Nothing secret lives here -- host names, LAN addresses and key *paths*. The keys
# themselves stay in ~/.ssh and are not in this repo and never will be.
#
# AddKeysToAgent sits before the first Host block deliberately: ssh applies the first
# value it obtains for a keyword, and settings outside any Host block apply globally. Move
# it below a Host block and it silently applies to that host alone.

AddKeysToAgent yes

# Local-only overrides and hosts that must not be in a PUBLIC repo: ~/.ssh/config.local.
# Relative Include paths resolve against ~/.ssh. Nothing secret belongs in this file OR in
# that one -- keys stay in ~/.ssh either way. What that file is for is the other category:
# real config that is simply nobody else's business, such as a Host block naming a routable
# address and User root, which in a public repo advertises a login target.
#
# Placed HERE deliberately, and the position is load-bearing in both directions. AFTER
# AddKeysToAgent, so that global value is obtained first and still applies to every host
# (ssh keeps the FIRST value it obtains for a keyword). BEFORE the first Host block, so a
# block in config.local can override one below rather than losing to it.
#
# A MISSING INCLUDE IS SILENT. ssh does not error on an absent included file, so on a host
# that has no config.local this simply defines nothing -- and the failure surfaces later as
# `Could not resolve hostname vps`. That is survivable because these are hosts reached by
# hand, but do not put anything load-bearing here expecting to be told when it is absent.
# Same hazard the umbriel include layering has, and for the same reason. See CLAUDE.md.
Include config.local

Host waylab
    HostName 192.168.1.209
    User peter
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_waylab
    IdentitiesOnly yes

Host github.com
    HostName github.com
    User git
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_github
    IdentitiesOnly yes

Host omada
    HostName 192.168.1.49
    User peter
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_homelab
    IdentitiesOnly yes

Host proxmox
    HostName 192.168.1.50
    User root
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_homelab
    IdentitiesOnly yes

# rigel -> caesar. caesar is keys-only for peter (hosts/caesar/ssh/10-nomarchy.conf), and
# its ~/.ssh/authorized_keys is deliberately NOT in this repo: a symlink into a public repo
# would make a push to GitHub a login grant on caesar. The key named here exists on rigel
# only; on caesar this block is inert.
#
# Off-site this still resolves: rigel reaches the home LAN over Tailscale. caesar's address
# is DHCP, so it holds only as long as the router keeps reserving it.
Host caesar
    HostName 192.168.1.200
    User peter
    AddressFamily inet
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_caesar
    IdentitiesOnly yes

